{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774127683,"nonce":"2C+LBrFdu5SCCb/lR7NCt4fkSRE=","title":"Channel mode terminal view: xterm.js for channel-connected sessions","message":"Channel mode sessions (claude --channels server:mandible) need a terminal view in the Console tab for permission prompt interaction. Currently TerminalPane only shows xterm.js when backendType === \"pty\". Channel sessions lack PermissionAwareBackend — the user must interact with Claude Code permission prompts in the terminal.\n\n## Problem\nChannel mode sessions have no terminal UI in Mandible. Without it, users running Claude Code without --dangerously-skip-permissions will hit blocking permission prompts with no way to respond.\n\n## Approach\n- Add a \"channel\" backend_type (or reuse PTY xterm.js for channel sessions)\n- The terminal view connects to the external Claude Code process via a PTY relay or WebSocket bridge\n- Three options for terminal data:\n  1. PTY relay: Mandible re-creates a PTY around the external process (not feasible — process is already running)\n  2. WebSocket bridge to the Claude CLI terminal output (requires CLI cooperation)\n  3. Script/expect wrapper: Launch `claude --channels server:mandible` from Mandible Console as a PTY backend with the channel flag, combining PTY terminal visibility with channel integration\n- Option 3 is most practical: treat channel mode as a \"Mandible-launched Claude CLI session with channel integration\" — PTY provides the terminal, channel provides the structured events\n\n## Dependencies\n- Channel server (73e0adf) — done\n- PTY backend — exists but was being deprecated for Claude sessions\n- ViewToggle.tsx and TerminalPane.tsx need conditional logic for channel mode\n\n## Interaction with PTY deprecation (ef4eb11)\nPTY deprecation was for SDK-replacing-PTY. Channel mode re-legitimizes PTY as the terminal transport for channel-connected sessions. The PTY carries terminal I/O while the channel carries structured events.","files":null}]}